meta {
  name: Seeding
  seq: 9
}

docs {
  **Only the user runs these requests. Never the assistant.**

  Every request in this folder MUTATES Linear state. They are authored here, with their
  real HTTP verb and real GraphQL `mutation` document visible, and handed to the user to
  run. The assistant does not execute them under any circumstance.

  Everything at the collection's top level is read-only (GraphQL `query` documents); this
  folder is the only place mutations live.

  ## Why this folder exists

  The Estuary workspace is Linear's stock onboarding content and nothing else:

  | collection | rows | note                                       |
  |------------|------|--------------------------------------------|
  | issues     | 4    | all share `updatedAt` 2026-07-30T21:35:03.808Z |
  | issueLabels| 3    | same timestamp; all workspace-level        |
  | projects   | 0    | endpoint never observed with data          |
  | initiatives| 0    | endpoint never observed with data          |
  | archived   | 0    | across all four types                      |

  That leaves four things unverifiable by reading alone. Each request below closes exactly
  one of them; the "re-run after" line names the read probe to re-execute afterwards.

  ## Run order

  `A1` and `A2` are independent of each other and of the `D` group. `D1` and `D2` both
  target an existing issue and should be run in order, D1 then D2, because D2's archival
  also re-answers D1's question.

  Cap: 4 mutations, all plain single requests, no loops.
}
